SPRINT 3 — DREAM ACTIVATION / DREAM ANCHOR
==========================================
STATUS: COMPLETE

Goal
----
Replace the temporary global activation boolean with an intentional
in-world mechanism so individual beds can opt into Dream gameplay
without replacing normal Minecraft sleeping.


Dream Anchor Prototype
----------------------
The current Dream Anchor is a custom registered block.

Working presentation:
    Gilded Pot

Current development appearance:
    Temporary amethyst-block model/texture

The full Gilded Pot model, collision shape, sounds, storage behavior,
and final assets are deferred to Sprint 4.


Activation Rule
---------------
A bed is Dream-enabled when a Dream Anchor exists within 3 blocks
of the bed.

Dream activation is evaluated around the specific bed being used.

The Anchor:
- is not consumed
- does not globally enable Dreaming
- does not bypass vanilla sleep restrictions


NO DREAM ANCHOR

Player uses bed
↓
Dream activation check fails
↓
Dream mod does nothing
↓
Vanilla sleeping proceeds normally


VALID DREAM ANCHOR

Player uses bed
↓
Dream Anchor exists within activation radius
↓
Vanilla validates sleep normally
↓
If vanilla rejects sleep:
    Dream does not start

If vanilla accepts sleep:
    Player enters valid vanilla sleep
    ↓
    Dream mod transitions player into Dream
    ↓
    Existing DreamService lifecycle handles entry, timer, persistence,
    and wake behavior


