FUTURE DESIGN CONSIDERATIONS
============================

Same-Night Dream Re-entry
-------------------------
Future rule:

After waking from a Dream, prevent that player from entering another
Dream during the same Minecraft night.

This primarily matters in multiplayer where another player may cause
the night to continue instead of immediately advancing to morning.

Exact "same night" semantics should be designed alongside future
night-progression behavior.


Night Progression
-----------------
Eventually determine how Dream completion interacts with Minecraft time.

Questions include:

- Should completing a Dream skip the night?
- Should waking advance time?
- What happens if another player sleeps while someone is Dreaming?
- What happens if morning arrives naturally?
- Should Dreamers remain inside the Dream after sunrise?
- How should playersSleepingPercentage interact with Dreaming?


Personal Dream Worlds
---------------------
The Dream is one persistent shared Minecraft dimension:

    dream:dream

Players do not receive separate ServerLevel/dimension instances.

Instead, each player owns one persistent personal region inside the
shared Dream dimension.

Each region:

- is 25 x 25 chunks
- is approximately 400 x 400 blocks
- uses normal Overworld-style world generation
- persists permanently between Dream visits
- may be built in and modified by its owner
- directly borders neighboring player regions
- is logically inaccessible to other players at the beginning


Dream Region Grid
-----------------
Personal Dream regions form a contiguous grid.

Example:

+---------+---------+---------+
| Player A| Player B| Player C|
| 25 x 25 | 25 x 25 | 25 x 25 |
+---------+---------+---------+
| Player D| Player E| Player F|
| 25 x 25 | 25 x 25 | 25 x 25 |
+---------+---------+---------+
| Player G| Player H| Player I|
| 25 x 25 | 25 x 25 | 25 x 25 |
+---------+---------+---------+

Each player permanently owns a grid coordinate:

    gridX
    gridZ

Region assignments should remain stable across:

- logout
- Save & Quit
- server restart
- future Dream visits


Region Allocation
-----------------
New player regions should be allocated outward from the existing
Dream community rather than extending forever in only one direction.

Preferred approach:
    outward-growing / spiral grid allocation

This keeps active player regions geographically clustered while
preserving direct neighboring relationships.


Terrain Continuity
------------------
All personal regions exist inside the same generated Dream dimension.

This means normal terrain can continue naturally across boundaries:

- rivers may cross between player regions
- caves may continue beneath borders
- mountain ranges may span multiple regions
- biomes may naturally continue across regions

The player ownership boundary is logical rather than a terrain seam.


Dream Borders
-------------
At the beginning of progression, players cannot cross the boundaries
of their assigned 25 x 25 chunk Dream region.

Borders should NOT permanently rely on physical bedrock/barrier walls.

Instead, border behavior should remain an abstract gameplay rule so
future technology can selectively permit interaction between neighbors.


Future Border Technology
------------------------
As Dream technology progresses, neighboring players may eventually
connect their regions across shared borders.

Possible future connections include:

- item transfer
- Forge Energy / RF transfer
- paired doors or gates
- authorized player travel

Early game:
    borders are completely sealed

Later game:
    specific technologies may permit controlled interaction between
    neighboring Dream regions.

The physical Dream grid therefore becomes part of multiplayer
progression rather than only an implementation detail.


